# The score blending with the land, from a normal game start on the south coast.
# It wakes with the coast and reaches its whole voice within half a minute; then
# the player is put in the moss in one step, far faster than any bake, and the
# coast keeps playing until the moss can take over (playtest 14: it used to fall
# silent). Then two borders walked with real input, each one two landscapes
# sounding at once. The last await fails the tour if the score was ever silent
# for longer than GAP_BUDGET since it first sounded.
# The log shows the blend it holds: "[coast 0.79 | moss 0.61] drone, pad ...".
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=900 tools/tour.sh tours/score-blend.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
await score 150
await score_full 120
shot 01-the-whole-score-in-half-a-minute
# Two hundred tiles north in one step: the moss takes the ear only as fast as
# it is baked, and the coast holds the rest of it meanwhile.
place moss
wait 3
shot 02-arrived-faster-than-the-bake
await score_here 240
shot 03-the-moss-took-over-without-a-gap with land:moss
# The first border, walked: the coast and the moss share a tonal centre, so the
# two keys lean into each other over the whole ecotone.
place coast-moss
await score_blend 180
shot 04-on-the-coast-moss-border with border:coast-moss
walk 0,1 7 run
walk 0,1 7 run
shot 05-walked-down-into-the-coast with land:coast
walk 0,-1 8 run
walk 0,-1 8 run
await score_blend 180
shot 06-walked-back-up-into-the-moss with land:moss
# The second border, walked: the pines are the coast's seven notes a fifth
# down, so this one leans too. East from the ecotone into the wood.
place moss-pinewood
await score_blend 180
shot 07-on-the-moss-pinewood-border with border:moss-pinewood
walk 0.71,0.71 7 run
walk 0.71,0.71 7 run
await score_in:pinewood 240
shot 08-walked-east-into-the-pines
await score_pad 240
shot 09-and-the-pines-fill-out
# Nothing above was heard over a hole in the score.
await score_unbroken 120
echo the score never fell silent
